<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Athanagild</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 567</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Athanagild was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> from 554 to 567. He rebelled against King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agila-i">Agila I</a> and sought help from the Byzantine emperor Justinian, whose forces then seized a coastal strip of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> his residence, and his daughters <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunhilda-of-austrasia">Brunhilda</a> and Galswintha married the Frankish kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigebert-i">Sigebert I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chilperic-i">Chilperic I</a>.</p></div>
